Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||02-26-2001||11:57 AM||||well, im finally gonna go to the boneyard to grab a new engine, and i was wondering- get a fiero 2.8 or a camaro 3.4? i have the engine install/removal down to about 8 hours, so i know how to do all that, but i was just wwondering what all i need to grab outta the car- engine, flywheel? im pulling it myself so im just gonna leave all the accs on it. do i need the camaro computer? (my car is 1987gt 5spd) also, would i put my fiero heads on there, or are the camaro ones better? and finally, are the tools for removing the fiero engine gonna be the same for the camaro? thanks for any responses. oh, i know the starter holes must be drilled, how hard is this, especially with the 2 engines side by side?||||reg||1
Z||000001||mshill||02-26-2001||12:14 PM||||You are going to have a fun time trying to find a 3.4L camaro engine in california.  They had to get mine from somewhere in the mid-west.<P>The heads are the same as the Fiero 2.8L.  Get the flywheel if it has one.  There are many using the stock fiero computer and stock fiero injectors on their 3.4Ls.<P>||||reg||1
